SSL has no truthy/falsy coercion: a literal string, number or NIL as an
:IF/:WHILE condition, or as the left operand of .AND./.OR., raises at run
time on v12. diag.non_logical_condition reports each literal (issue
#322); the same condition written with a variable is not provable and
stays silent by design.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Gate;
	:PARAMETERS bOpen;
	:DECLARE bOut;
	bOut := .F.;
	:IF "x";
		bOut := .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:WHILE 1;
		:EXITWHILE;
	:ENDWHILE;
	bOut := "x" .AND. bOpen;
	bOut := 0 .OR. bOut;
	:RETURN bOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Gate;
	:PARAMETERS bOpen;
	:DECLARE bOut;

	bOut := .F.;

	:IF "x";
		bOut := .T.;
	:ENDIF;

	:WHILE 1;
		:EXITWHILE;
	:ENDWHILE;

	bOut := "x" .AND. bOpen;
	bOut := 0 .OR. bOut;

	:RETURN bOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:6-5:9 error non_logical_condition: ':IF' condition is a string literal - SSL has no truthy/falsy coercion, so a non-logical condition raises at run time
8:9-8:10 error non_logical_condition: ':WHILE' condition is a number literal - SSL has no truthy/falsy coercion, so a non-logical condition raises at run time
11:10-11:13 error non_logical_condition: Left operand of '.AND.' is a string literal - '.AND.' and '.OR.' raise at run time on a non-logical left operand
12:10-12:11 error non_logical_condition: Left operand of '.OR.' is a number literal - '.AND.' and '.OR.' raise at run time on a non-logical left operand
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:6-5:9 error non_logical_condition: ':IF' condition is a string literal - SSL has no truthy/falsy coercion, so a non-logical condition raises at run time
8:9-8:10 error non_logical_condition: ':WHILE' condition is a number literal - SSL has no truthy/falsy coercion, so a non-logical condition raises at run time
11:10-11:13 error non_logical_condition: Left operand of '.AND.' is a string literal - '.AND.' and '.OR.' raise at run time on a non-logical left operand
12:10-12:11 error non_logical_condition: Left operand of '.OR.' is a number literal - '.AND.' and '.OR.' raise at run time on a non-logical left operand
